  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Tuesday will be the coolest day this week, with \npatchy frost possible again Tuesday night.\n\nLight winds, clear skies, and low dewpoints have resulted in\neffective radiational cooling over west central PA, with temps\nas low as the upper 20s and low 30s this morning. Temperatures\nwill moderate during the day under abundant sunshine. Undercut\nthe NBM for dewpoints this afternoon given the dry airmass and \neffective mixing. \n\nHigh pressure will slide east through the day into tonight, \nwith winds shifting around to the SW across west central PA. \nThis should make frost less likely tonight in the places that \nwere coldest this morning. However, frost will be possible to \nthe east where winds will be calm, closer to the center of the \nhigh.\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n \nKEY MESSAGE 2: Extended stretch of dry and seasonal Fall \nweather this week, followed by a chance of rain on Sunday.\n\nHigh confidence in a prolonged stretch of dry and seasonable \nFall wx this week with cool nights and refreshing afternoons \nwith low humidity. This will give the area a much needed chance \nto dry out from the wet summer and early fall so far.\n\nThe next chance of rain is on Sunday, as moisture moves up from\nthe Gulf Coast states. However, there is still ample uncertainty\nregarding how much of that moisture makes it into our region.",
